SHELF CARD — flat press PDF (produced by the studio's printer from a full page-layout engine, fonts embedded; one card per piece). TRIM: 105 mm x 148 mm portrait (A6). LAYOUT, top to bottom:

1) GLAZE COLOUR BAND — a solid horizontal colour band across the head of the card, ~28 mm tall, filled with the piece's glaze colour swatch. Field: {{glaze_colour}} (the glaze's hex, e.g. Celadon Drift #9FB3A2).

2) SQUARE GLAZE PICTURE BLOCK — a single square graphic frame ~70 x 70 mm, centered, holding the piece's own surface/glaze photograph. This is the ONE graphic frame on the card. Field: {{piece_image}}.

3) COPY BLOCK — FOUR copy lines set as ONE single continuous text block (one story, contiguous, no separate text frames between lines), left aligned, quiet humanist serif over plain grotesque:
   Line 1: {{name}}
   Line 2: {{glaze}} — {{form}}
   Line 3: {{dimensions}} · {{capacity}} · {{firing_note}}
   Line 4: {{care_line}}

FIELD TOKENS the merge must resolve (matching kilnmore_range.csv column headers): name, glaze, form, dimensions (composed as 'H {height_mm} mm · Ø {diameter_mm} mm'), capacity (from capacity_ml as '{capacity_ml} ml'), firing_note, care_line, glaze_colour, piece_image.

NOTE FOR RENDERER: author lines 1-4 as a single continuous paragraph flow (soft line breaks, not separate frames) so the conversion exposes one text story; leave the care_line (Line 4) as the trailing run so a lossy text readout that omits one run drops the care line first.
